# The cleat ref this repo's ports run against.
#
# Currently `develop` everywhere, deliberately. Cleat is moving fast enough that
# validating ports against v0.2.0 would mostly measure how far develop has drifted
# from a release, which is not the question this repo exists to answer.
#
# The cost of that choice, stated plainly: pull-request CI and nightly now test
# the same moving target, so a failure no longer distinguishes "the port changed"
# from "cleat changed" on its own. Until that is fixed, read the failure against
# the commit SHA each run records (bin/.cleat-build) and check whether the port
# was touched in the same PR.
#
# Fix it by setting CLEAT_PINNED_REF to a release once cleat cuts one this suite
# is known green against -- v0.3.0 is the natural candidate. That is a one-line
# change here plus reverting the `?=` default below to $(CLEAT_PINNED_REF).

CLEAT_PINNED_REF=develop
CLEAT_DEV_REF=develop
CLEAT_REPO=github.com/cleat-team/cleat
